## Project Analysis
- matmul_1: 24576x768 × 768x384 = 24576x384 (f64) - Very tall, narrow result
- matmul_2: 512x512 × 512x512 = 512x512 (f64) - Square, medium
- matmul_3: 256x512 × 512x1024 = 256x1024 (f64) - Wide result (no PyTorch bench)
- All operations use f64 (double precision)
- Target: AVX2 with 4-wide doubles, FMA, Broadwell Xeon E5-2680 v4
- 28 cores, 2 NUMA nodes

## Hardware Notes for f64
- AVX2 vector width: 4 doubles (256 bits)
- L1: 32KB per core → ~32×32 tile for 3 matrices of f64
- L2: 256KB per core → ~128×128 tile
- L3: 35MB shared → large tiles
- FMA: 2 FMA units per cycle on Broadwell
- Peak: 8 double-precision FLOPs/cycle/core

## Existing Schedules Analysis
- main_1: Parallel(512 M), K=128+promoteA, N=64+promoteB, micro=4×8, vectorize
- main_2: Parallel(128×128), K=128+promoteA, N=64+promoteB, micro=4×8, vectorize
- tmp_1: BLIS-like: Parallel(384 M), K=256+promoteA, N=96+promoteB, micro=6×8×1, unroll K×8
- llm_2: Parallel(128 M), K=64+promote(A,B), micro=4×16×1, generalize+vectorize, unroll K×8

