## Session 3 - Round 14+ (claude30+): use_alloca & Alignment Breakthrough

KEY DISCOVERY: `transform.structured.promote` has a `use_alloca` attribute that creates
memref.alloca (stack) instead of memref.alloc (malloc) DIRECTLY, bypassing the
promote-buffers-to-stack limitation. Also discovered `alignment = 64` attribute for
AVX2-aligned buffers.

IMPORTANT CAVEAT: memref.alloca inside scf.for loops grows the stack each iteration!
The alloca is NOT hoisted by LLVM -O3 when inside a loop body. This means:
- A panel alloca (294KB) inside K-loop × 4 iters = ~1.2MB stack growth
- B panel alloca (73KB) inside N-loop × 8 iters = ~584KB more
- Total stack per thread: ~1.8MB (still within typical 4-8MB limit but cache-unfriendly)

