## Session 15: No-Promotion Breakthrough (claude128-claude149)

### Key Discovery: Eliminating ALL promotion dramatically improves matmul_1
After 14 sessions of exhaustive optimization, discovered that removing all data copying
(no A promotion, no B promotion) for the tall matmul_1 is actually FASTER than explicit
BLIS-style data packing. This is because:
1. Each thread's A-slice (128×64×8=64KB) is accessed sequentially → hardware prefetch friendly
2. B matrix (768×384×8=2.25MB) shared across threads in L3 → no per-thread copy needed
3. Eliminates ALL malloc/free/memrefCopy overhead (significant with 28 threads × 6 K-iters)

