### Key Technical Findings
1. KR=8 is optimal — larger KR causes register pressure (16 YMM regs on Broadwell)
2. matmulintrinsics crashes LLC (LLVM matrix intrinsics bug)
3. transpose_matmul requires tensor IR and loses op tags after transformation
4. noalias injection at MLIR level doesn't propagate through OpenMP outlining
5. matmul_2 copy loops (~41% of time) are likely optimized by ExecutionEngine(opt_level=3)
6. Both matmuls assembly is already very tight: 64 FMA + 8 C stores per K=8 iteration

