### Bottleneck Analysis
Memory operations dominate the inner loop: 88 load/stores vs 64 FMAs per micro-kernel invocation.
With 2 load ports + 1 store port → ~40 cycles for memory, 32 cycles for FMAs → memory-bound.
FMA utilization: 64/(40×2) = 80% — matches observed 80% of peak for matmul_2.
MKL achieves >90% likely due to:
1. JIT-compiled micro-kernels with perfect instruction scheduling
2. Software prefetching (we have no way to insert prefetch hints)
3. Hardware-aware thread pool (vs OpenMP overhead)
4. Turbo boost optimization (single burst call)

