### Assembly Analysis (matmul_2 inner loop)
Per K=8 step: 16 B loads + 32 A broadcasts + 3 explicit C loads + 5 fused C-in-FMA + 8 C stores = 64 mem ops, 64 FMAs
C reloaded every K-iteration due to LLVM aliasing concerns (C may alias promoted A/B allocas)
Memory port pressure: 56 loads / 2 ports = 28 cycles, 8 stores / 1 port = 8 cycles, FMAs: 64 / 2 = 32 cycles
Slightly compute-bound at instruction level — 80% gap is likely from TLB misses on strided C access

