## Session 61 (Iteration 1299-1306)

### Bug Fix: SO Runner SIGSEGV
- Root cause 1: Extra exec_time arg passed to _mlir_ciface_main (function returns i64, doesn't take 4th arg)
- Root cause 2: Wrong pointer level — ciface takes ptr-to-struct, not ptr-to-ptr-to-struct
- Fix: `ctypes.pointer(get_ranked_memref_descriptor(arr))` instead of `ctypes.pointer(ctypes.pointer(...))`
- SO runner now works for ALL matmuls (verified locally: m1=709ms/1thread, m2=14.8ms, m3=14.1ms)

### Key Finding: SO Runner (opt -O3 + llc -mcpu=broadwell) provides NO advantage over JIT
- m1 SO: 1.61x vs JIT -opt: 1.62x — SAME
- m2 SO+fpc: 1.52x vs JIT+fpc: 1.43x — JIT 7% BETTER
- m3 SO-noalias+fpc: 1.29x vs JIT-noalias+fpc: 1.14x — JIT 13% BETTER
- JIT already detects host CPU as broadwell

