KEY DISCOVERIES:
1. tensor.pad + hoist_pad WORKS for hoisting packing outside K-loop, but
   nofold creates unavoidable zero-fill + double-copy overhead (4-5x WORSE with alloca)
2. promote-before-K successfully moves A packing outside K-loop, enabling -opt LICM
   for m2 (previously -opt HURT m2). But 128KB A panel offsets the LICM gain.
3. loop-versioning-licm adds runtime overhead that negates benefit
4. The fundamental trade-off: packing inside K-loop hurts LICM but gives smaller panels;
   packing outside K-loop enables LICM but requires larger panels
5. Current baseline configs (KC=256 + promote inside K) are at the optimal balance point

