--- KC=512 Full-K Results (m2) ---
Hypothesis: Full K=512 (no KC tiling) keeps C in registers across full K dimension
A promote: 32×512×8 = 128KB (L2), B promote: 512×8×8 = 32KB (L1)

Job 14096305: claude1536_2 standard (postRA+fpc) → 631ns / 377ns PyTorch = 1.675x WORSE
Job 14096306: claude1536_2 noalias (postRA+fpc) → 620ns / 381ns PyTorch = 1.625x WORSE
Job 14096307: claude1536_2 -opt (postRA+fpc)    → 596ns / 381ns PyTorch = 1.562x WORSE

CONCLUSION: KC=512 is significantly WORSE. 128KB A promote overflows L1 (32KB),
causing massive L1 cache misses that outweigh C register hoisting benefit.
Confirms KC=256 is optimal for m2 (A panel = 64KB fits L2, not L1 either, but smaller footprint).

