--- Vector Lowering Strategy Research ---
- outerproduct: OPTIMAL for AVX2 matmul (32 vfmadd per K=8 contraction)
- dot: terrible (horizontal reductions = expensive shuffle chains)
- matmulintrinsics: gives up tiling control to LLVM
- parallelarith: only works when K=1, not applicable

CONCLUSIONS SESSION 73:
- K=1+unroll approach is fundamentally worse than K=8 vectorize
- K=8 vectorize already keeps C in SSA registers within each K-block
- The C reload bottleneck is at K-block BOUNDARIES, not within blocks
- No MLIR-level fix exists (would need custom LLVM pass or iter_args)
- NUMA, thread configs, pipeline passes: all NEUTRAL
- Current configurations are at a hard optimum for MLIR transform dialect

