--- Software Pipeline Experiments (Batch 86: jobs 14097345-14097353) ---

Tried transform.loop.pipeline on three loops:
1. claude1564_2: pipeline K-inner (K=8 step) → INCORRECT RESULTS (192 vs 2048)
2. claude1565_2: pipeline KC (K=256 step) → GARBAGE/NaN values  
3. claude1566_2: pipeline NC (N=8 step) → GARBAGE/NaN values

All produce incorrect results. Software pipelining after full vector lowering
is unsafe — the complex SCF/memref/vector operations in the loop body are not
properly handled by the pipeline transform. The loop body references alloca
buffers that get incorrectly transformed into iter_args.

CONCLUSION: transform.loop.pipeline is NOT viable for our matmul schedules.

