SESSION 75 - Tensor-Land Scheduling & Vectorized Copy (Feb 16, 2026)
================================================================================

Research Focus: Novel approaches — tensor-land pad+hoist_pad, multibuffer, vectorized copy

--- Multibuffer Research ---
Finding: transform.memref.multibuffer requires memref.alloc (not alloca) that DOMINATES the loop
         promote creates alloc INSIDE the loop body → multibuffer is structurally inapplicable
         Multibuffer solves a problem (loop-carried reuse) that doesn't exist with per-iteration allocs
Status: NOT APPLICABLE — structural mismatch with promote

--- Tensor-Land Pad+Hoist Pipeline Fix ---
Problem: tensor.pad nofold → memref.copy (strided) → @memrefCopy → unrealized_conversion_cast
Root cause: vector.transfer_read/write ops survive into OpenMP outlined function
Fix: Added convert-vector-to-scf{full-unroll=true} BEFORE scf-forall-to-parallel
Also needed: promote-buffers-to-stack{max-alloc-size-in-bytes=1048576 max-rank-of-allocated-memref=4}
Also needed: replace memref.copy → linalg.copy via text substitution (run_tensorpad.py)
Status: FIXED — all 3 matmuls compile cleanly with new pipeline

--- Batch 94: Tensor-Land Pad+Hoist (14100052-14100059) ---
Schedule: claude1583_{1,2,3} (pad+hoist A out of K loop)
Pipeline: claude1583 pipeline with convert-vector-to-scf, promote-buffers-to-stack
Run via: -tensorpad flag (uses run_tensorpad.py for memref.copy→linalg.copy conversion)

Results:
14100052: m1 pad+hoist A    → 1.649x (MUCH WORSE vs best 1.17x)
14100053: m2 pad-only        → 1.920x (WORSE vs best 1.39x)
14100054: m2 pad+hoist A     → 2.025x (WORSE)
14100055: m2 pad+hoist A+B   → 2.473x (MUCH WORSE)
14100056: m3 pad+hoist A     → 1.765x (WORSE vs best 1.10x)
14100057: m2 baseline        → 1.396x (baseline ✓)
14100058: m3 baseline        → 1.095x (baseline ✓)
14100059: m1 baseline        → 1.180x (baseline ✓)

Analysis: tensor-land pad+hoist is DEFINITIVELY WORSE than memref promote:
- Zero-fill (linalg.map) from padding is redundant overhead
- Intermediate temp buffer from pad → double copy overhead
- linalg.copy from memref.copy text replacement creates slower loop-based copies
- More hoisting = more overhead (A+B worst, A-only worst for no-B case)

