--- Batch 96: Vectorized Copy (14100064-14100067) ---
Schedule: claude1586 — same tiling/promote as best, but linalg.copy vectorized
  transform.structured.vectorize applied to linalg.copy ops
  Creates vector.transfer_read + vector.transfer_write for 32x256 and 256x8 copies
  Pipeline has convert-vector-to-scf{full-unroll=true} before OpenMP

Results:
14100064: m2 vec-copy + fpc        → 2.064x (WORSE — code bloat from full unroll)
14100065: m3 vec-copy + noalias    → 1.517x (WORSE — 307 loads annotated vs 21 baseline)
14100066: m2 vec-copy, no-fpc      → 1.943x (WORSE)
14100067: m1 vec-copy + opt        → ERROR (pipeline file missing during job submission)

Analysis: Vectorizing linalg.copy creates 32 individual vector.load + 32 vector.store
for 32x256 panel, which is ~1500 lines of IR (vs ~200 with scalar loops).
LLVM JIT at opt_level=3 already vectorizes scalar copy loops effectively.
Explicit vectorization just adds code bloat → WORSE performance.

