=== Session 78-79: C Promotion, External Compilation, Direct LLC ===

Key experiments:
- opt -O3 promotes C accumulators to registers (4 phi nodes, 32 fmuladd)
  - Targeted LICM: function(sroa,instcombine,loop-simplify,lcssa,loop-mssa(licm))
  - Achieves same C promotion as full O3 with minimal passes
  - But ALL reimport pipelines WORSE due to reimport overhead (1.49-1.70x for m2)
- Direct LLC compilation (mlir→translate→opt→LLC→.o→.so→dlopen):
  - Avoids MLIR reimport entirely
  - LLC REQUIRES -mcpu=broadwell for AVX2 (without: 3-5x slower!)
  - m2 direct O3+mcpu: 1.509x (worse than 1.39x JIT)
  - m3 direct-noalias O3+mcpu: 1.104x (near tie with 1.10x best)
  - Conclusion: JIT is near-optimal for all matmuls
- Deep assembly analysis confirmed:
  - JIT uses vfmadd213pd with memory source (load-fused FMA)
  - C loads are essentially "free" at start of inner loop
  - 64 FMAs per KR=8 iteration, 8 C stores after
  - LLC assembly: 8 C accumulators in ymm0-7, 32 FMAs, vmovapd for B

Batch 112 (LICM): ALL WORSE (1.31-1.70x)
